# NEVER COMMITTED.  `secrets/` is 0700 and holds every generated value;
# `.env` holds the rendered pin block and the database passwords.
#
# The mode on `secrets/` is 0700 owned by the OPERATOR, not by root: it holds
# root-owned per-service files, and the operator has to be able to traverse it
# or compose cannot read any env_file (MEASURED, NOM-258 — see gen-secrets.sh).
secrets/
.env
.runtime/
backups/
config/authelia/users.yml
config/image-facts.yaml.bak
*.bak
.backup-keys-confirmed

# GENERATED, NEVER COMMITTED — and this one is load-bearing, not tidiness.
#
# MEASURED (NOM-258, 2026-10-18): three `security-report-*/invariants.txt`
# files were committed, and invariant I6 scans every file `git ls-files`
# reports for banned strings.  A saved report PRINTS I6's own description,
# which names the banned browser sandbox flag — so the report contained it,
# and I6 FAILED on a clean clone of HEAD.  CI red for no reason but the repo
# shipping its own scan output.  The working tree passed only because someone
# had deleted those files locally without committing the deletion, which is
# the worst version of this: green where the build runs, red where anyone
# else checks it out.
#
# This comment deliberately does NOT quote the flag.  It was written with the
# literal first, and I6 failed on THIS file — correctly.  The fix is prose
# that describes the string, not a third entry in I6's self-exclusion list.
security-report-*/
support-bundle-*.tar.gz
drill-log.txt
install.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# GENERATED BY `aistack samples setup`, AND THE POINT IS THAT IT IS NOT HERE.
#
# samples/fixtures/make-synthetic-pdf.py writes synthetic.pdf deterministically
# on every run.  Committing the output would give the repo a binary with no
# reviewable diff — "the PDF changed" is a line nobody can read — in the single
# most attacker-shaped file format this stack accepts.  The generator is the
# artefact under review; the file is a build product, and `samples teardown`
# deletes it.
#
# samples/.run/ is the scratch directory the demo credentials pass through on
# their way into n8n (0600, removed on EXIT).  It lives under samples/ only
# because that is the one path bind-mounted into the n8n container.
samples/fixtures/synthetic.pdf
samples/.run/

# THE GATE MUST NOT BE ABLE TO COMMIT ITS OWN OUTPUT — and this block has
# already been lost once.  4345e96 added it; f98b0c6 rewrote the tail of this
# file and took it away with no mention in its message, so for a day
# `ci/scan-gate.py` left an untracked 110KB gate.json in the repo root where
# any `git add -A` from a neighbouring change would have committed it.
# `ci/scan-gate.py` writes gate.json unless GATE_JSON names somewhere else.
# Ignored for the same reason as security-report-*/ above, and I6 now ASSERTS
# this entry is here rather than trusting that nobody deletes it again.
gate.json
